  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 127 AM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nTuesday features a Marginal severe threat over the eastern\nOzarks for the afternoon. This would likely be due to diurnal\nheating processes with damaging wind gusts and an isolated \nbrief tornado possible. This severe threat will be conditional\nand could be impacted by any cloud cover from the overnight\nconvection. \n\nThe low pressure system that moves through at the beginning of\nthe week will drop our temperatures, but only by about 10\ndegrees. Though, it will bring them closer to average for this\ntime of year with highs in the 60s and lows in the 40s for the\nrest of the week. Cloud cover starts to dissipate on Wednesday\nand skies remain partly cloudy to mostly sunny into the \nweekend. All of the low-end (15-20%) chances for rain previously\nmentioned for the end of the week have disappeared. Our air \nmass may be too dry for those rain showers to form as surface \nhigh pressure moves in for the middle to end of the week.",
